drydock-hail-service = Drydock services

drydock-hail-greeting-1 = Aye, { $location }, { $name } here. Speak up, { $ship }!
drydock-hail-greeting-2 = { $name } o' { $location }, by me beard. Whit d'ye need, { $ship }?
drydock-hail-greeting-3 = Och, another hull! { $location } dockmaster. Go on then, { $ship }.

drydock-hail-offer = Open the drydock services an' tell me whit she needs. Ah'll find ye a berth.
drydock-hail-booked = Berth { $berth } is yers. Get her in there, hold her still, an' the cranes'll start swingin'.
drydock-hail-working = Me cranes are on yer ship in berth { $berth }. { $minutes } min more. Dinnae rush good work.

drydock-dockmaster-greeting = Aye? Dockmaster's desk. Whit can Ah dae fer ye?
drydock-dockmaster-farewell = Mind the cranes, an' mind yer heid.
drydock-dockmaster-prompt-how = How does the drydock work?
drydock-dockmaster-response-how = Hail me an' Ah'll find ye a berth that fits, or pull up tae a berth console yersel'. Follow the green lights in an' hold her still. Ye pay when the cranes start, an' whit they cannae finish or reach, ye get back.
drydock-dockmaster-prompt-hail = Do I have to come in person?
drydock-dockmaster-response-hail = Nae need tae walk! Hail me fae yer helm an' pick drydock services.
drydock-dockmaster-prompt-who = Who are you?
drydock-dockmaster-response-who = Hammer Ironstrike, dockmaster o' Anvilhold. Forty years swingin' cranes an' Ah've nae dropped a hull yet. Touch iron.
